3. Body weight ≥ 50 kg, BMI: 19.0-26.0 kg/m2 (inclusive);
4. Normal or abnormal but clinically insignificant results of vital signs, physical examination, laboratory tests (routine hematology, blood biochemistry, coagulation function, routine urinalysis, thyroid function, routine stool test + occult blood, etc.), 12-lead ECG, chest X-ray (posterior-anterior), and abdominal B-mode ultrasound (liver, gallbladder, pancreas, spleen, kidney, bladder);
